    "Q10.6": "Discussing with peers who also have non-standard study paths made me realize that 'prediction' often just means predicting the average, which excludes us. The idea of shifting from predictive surveillance to universal design was a key insight I hadn't considered before: support should be default, not conditional on being flagged."
